Subject: [PATCH 036/913] dt-bindings: add RISAFSUBPROT description for
 reserved memories

Add RISAF subregion macro description in st,protreg property.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git ce7ce685db681ccb00fb317755c5f2bcb6c187d8 dt-bindings: add RISAFSUBPROT description for reserved memories]
Signed-off-by: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I38ff4d4ef4a5561870caeb0733d20d33cac79c70
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/443823
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
Tested-by: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
---
 .../reserved-memory/reserved-memory.yaml      | 139 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 139 insertions(+)

diff --git a/documentation/devicetree/bindings/reserved-memory/reserved-memory.yaml b/documentation/devicetree/bindings/reserved-memory/reserved-memory.yaml
index c680e397c..080d9ad09 100644
--- a/documentation/devicetree/bindings/reserved-memory/reserved-memory.yaml
+++ b/documentation/devicetree/bindings/reserved-memory/reserved-memory.yaml
@@ -93,6 +93,145 @@ properties:
       system can use that region to store volatile or cached data that
       can be otherwise regenerated or migrated elsewhere.
 
+  st,protreg:
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 16
+    $ref: "/schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array"
+    description:
+      Describes the firewall hardware configuration to apply for the region.
+      This configuration will be applied by the firewall controller. The macro
+      used to describe the content of the configuration varies. It depends
+      on the type of the firewall controller.
+
+      -RISAF-
+      RISAFPROT(risaf_region, cid_read_list, cid_write_list,
+                cid_priv_list, sec, enc, enabled)
+
+        When a field isn't effective, it should be filled with RIF_UNUSED.
+
+        "risaf_region" Contains the ID of the RISAF region x to configure.
+          RISAF_REG_ID(x), region ID is x.
+
+        "cid_read_list" Contains the CID grantlist that can read the content
+                        of the region (multiple choice allowed).
+          RIF_CID1_BF | RIF_CID2_BF allows both CID 1/2 to read the region
+
+        "cid_write_list" Contains the CID grantlist that can write the
+                         content of the region (multiple choice allowed).
+          RIF_CID1_BF | RIF_CID4_BF allows both CID 1/4 to write in the region
+
+        "cid_priv_list" Defines compartments for which the access to the region
+                        is granted when the accesser is privileged
+                        (multiple choice allowed).
+          RIF_CID1_BF, Compartment 1 can access this region in privileged mode
+                       only. Others can access it, whatever their privilege
+                       state
+
+        "sec" Makes the region secure, if set.
+          RIF_SEC, region is accessible from secure world only
+          RIF_NSEC, region is accessible from non-secure world only
+
+        "enc" States that the region is encrypted.
+          RIF_ENC_DIS, encryption is disabled
+          RIF_ENC_EN, encryption is enabled
+
+        "enabled" Enables the region. Access controls applies.
+          RIF_BREN_DIS, region disabled
+          RIF_BREN_EN, region enabled
+
+      RISAFSUBPROT(risaf_subregion, dccid, dcen, rden, wren, srcid,
+                   priv, sec, enabled, rlock)
+
+        When a field isn't effective, it should be filled with RIF_UNUSED.
+
+        "risaf_subregion" Contains the ID of the RISAF subregion x to configure.
+          RISAF_SUBREG_ID(x), subregion ID is x.
+
+        "dccid" Contains the CID to which the subregion configuration is
+                delegated. This field has no effect in case of RIF_DCCID_DIS.
+          RIF_CIDx, subregion configuration is delegated to CID x
+
+        "dcen" The subregion configuration is delegated, if set.
+          RIF_DCCID_DIS, subregion delegation disabled
+          RIF_DCCID_EN, subregion delegation enabled
+
+        "rden" Read is enabled in the subregion for the CID defined in the
+               srcid field, if set.
+          RIF_RDEN_DIS, read in subregion disabled
+          RIF_RDEN_EN, read in subregion enabled
+
+        "wren" Write is enabled in the subregion for the CID defined in the
+               srcid field, if set.
+          RIF_WREN_DIS, write in subregion disabled
+          RIF_WREN_EN, write in subregion enabled
+
+        "srcid" Contains the CID which has access to the subregion.
+          RIF_CIDx, CID x has access to the subregion
+
+        "priv" Configures the privilege configuration for this subregion.
+          RIF_PRIV, Only privileged access is granted to the memory subregion
+          RIF_NPRIV, Privileged/Unprivileged access is granted to the memory
+                     subregion
+
+        "sec" Makes the subregion secure, if set.
+          RIF_SEC, subregion is accessible from secure world only
+          RIF_NSEC, subregion is accessible from non-secure world only
+
+        "enabled" Enables the subregion. Access controls applies.
+          RIF_SREN_DIS, subregion disabled
+          RIF_SREN_EN, subregion enabled
+
+        "rlock" The subregion resource is locked, if set.
+          RIF_RLOCK_DIS, subregion resource not locked
+          RIF_RLOCK_EN, subregion resource locked
+
+      -RISAB-
+      RISABPROT(delegate_en, delegate_cid, sec, default_priv, enabled,
+                cid_read_list, cid_write_list, cid_priv_list)
+
+        When a field isn't effective, it should be filled with RIF_UNUSED.
+
+        "delegate_en" The region configuration is delegated, if set. To be
+                      effective, it mandates that CID filtering is enabled.
+          RIF_DDCID_DIS, delegation disabled
+          RIF_DDCID_EN, delegation enabled
+
+        "delegate_cid" Contains the CID to which the configuration is delegated.
+          RIF_CIDx, configuration is delegated to CID x.
+
+        "sec" Configures secure-only access to the memory pages of this regions.
+          RIF_SEC, Only secure access is granted to the memory region.
+          RIF_NSEC, Only non-secure access is granted to the memory region.
+                    Secure access can be granted. See RISAB documentation.
+
+        "default_priv" Configures the default privilege configuration for this
+                      region (when CID filtering is disabled).
+          RIF_PRIV, Only privileged access is granted to the memory region
+          RIF_NPRIV, Privileged/Unprivileged access is granted to the memory
+                     region
+
+        "enabled" Enables the CID filtering for the region.
+          RIF_CFDIS, the CID filtering is disabled.
+          RIF_CFEN, the CID filtering is enabled.
+
+        "cid_read_list" Contains the CID grantlist that can read the content
+                        of the region (multiple choice allowed). Mandates CID
+                        filtering enabled to be effective.
+          RIF_CID1_BF | RIF_CID2_BF allows both CID 1/2 to read the region
+
+        "cid_write_list" Contains the CID grantlist that can write the
+                         content of the region (multiple choice allowed).
+                         Mandates CID filtering enabled to be effective.
+          RIF_CID1_BF | RIF_CID4_BF allows both CID 1/4 to write in the region.
+
+        "cid_priv_list" Defines compartments for which the access to the region
+                        is granted when the accesser is privileged (multiple
+                        choice allowed). Mandates CID filtering enabled to be
+                        effective.
+          RIF_CID1_BF, Compartment 1 can access this region in privileged mode
+                       only. Others can access it, whatever their privilege
+                       state
+
 allOf:
   - if:
       required:
